.TH MYSTRCMP 3 "November 2026" "libmyutils 0.4.1" "libmyutils Manual"
.SH NAME
mystrcmp \- compare two strings lexicographically
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <mystrfunctions.h>
.sp
.BI "int mystrcmp(const char *" str1 ", const char *" str2 );
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B mystrcmp
function compares the two null-terminated strings
.I str1
and
.I str2
character by character, in the style of the standard
.BR strcmp (3).
.PP
.B NULL
arguments are handled defensively: if both are
.BR NULL ,
they are considered equal; if only one is
.BR NULL ,
it is treated as lexicographically smaller than the non-NULL string.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns an integer less than, equal to, or greater than zero if
.I str1
is found, respectively, to be less than, to match, or be greater than
.IR str2 .
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
#include <mystrfunctions.h>
#include <stdio.h>

int main(void) {
    int r = mystrcmp("apple", "banana");
    if (r < 0)
        printf("apple comes before banana\en");
    return 0;
}
.fi
.SH AUTHOR
Written as part of the OS Assignment 01: Core C Utilities Library.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR strcmp (3)
